    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`, as a derived read-only field on the owner response.\n\nChanges, each placed where the concern already lives:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` enum (`EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` response schema, alongside the other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.). The DTO and its `ContactPreferenceEnum` are generated from this.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `hasEmail()` method as the single source of truth for \"email present\" (non-null, non-empty).\n\n3. **`MembershipLevels.java`** \u2014 Refactored its inline email check to reuse `owner.hasEmail()` instead of duplicating the logic.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a small `contactPreference(Owner)` derivation method wired via `@Mapping` expression, mirroring the existing derivation pattern (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `locality`, \u2026), reusing `hasEmail()`.\n\nThe derivation lives in the mapper next to the other owner-response derivations, and the email-presence rule is defined once on the entity and reused, so no class became a catch-all.",
